  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "ordered-reception",
      "claim": "ON_TAKE_DAMAGE actions modify a shared pending Modifier; shielding, multipliers, reflection and split are not universal separate stages. Priority and registration order affect observable results.",
      "basis": [
        "PRTS 伤判效果",
        "native BlockDamage/Evade/DamageSplit",
        "existing case 03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hit-sp-before-buff-reception",
      "claim": "Ordinary native Entity.OnTakeDamage attempts HIT SP recovery before BuffContainer.OnTakeDamage. It checks cancellation and the per-request ignoreForSp byte first.",
      "anchors": [
        "0x1806fa6c5",
        "0x1806fa6d2",
        "0x1806fa739",
        "0x1806fa772"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zero-input-vs-zero-hp-loss",
      "claim": "Modifier.get_isCancelled returns true for deltaType NONE or a zero value. ApplyModifier rejects an already-cancelled input before normal reception, so an initially zero-valued damage does not enter the ordinary HIT SP path. This differs from a positive damage cancelled by a later shield.",
      "anchors": [
        "0x1808b40d6",
        "0x1808b412e",
        "0x1806efe6e",
        "0x1806efe75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cancellation-permission",
      "claim": "Modifier.Cancel returns false if already cancelled or CheckIgnoreCancel forbids the requested reason. It does not zero the numeric value when cancellation succeeds; cancellation and value are separate state.",
      "anchors": [
        "0x1808b0ae4",
        "0x1808b0b0a",
        "0x1808b0b30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evade-attempt-vs-success",
      "claim": "Ordinary native Evade performs qualification and a probability check, then calls Cancel(EVADE). Only a successful cancellation enters OnEvadeDamage and writes the changed local Modifier back. No inference is made about every hotfixed or custom evade mechanism.",
      "anchors": [
        "0x18103d5d9",
        "0x18103d5f0",
        "0x18103d61e",
        "0x18103d625",
        "0x18103d668"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reflection-before-hp",
      "claim": "mlynar_t_2[inverse] runs InverseDamage in event 10 with filterModifierCancelled=false. Native InverseDamage synchronously constructs and applies another Modifier. Reflection can therefore occur inside reception before the outer HP application, and need not require outer HP loss.",
      "anchors": [
        "0x18105907b",
        "0x18105930e"
      ],
      "template": "mlynar_t_2[inverse]"
    },
    {
      "id": "shield-followup",
      "claim": "Mudrock shield event 10 is BlockDamage, HealViaMaxHpRatio(ignoreHealFree=true), presentation, FinishBuff. Cancelling the incoming damage is not a rollback of shield consumption or nested healing.",
      "template": "mudrok_t_1[shield_a]"
    },
    {
      "id": "split-is-nested-special-reception",
      "claim": "Skadi S1 protect invokes DamageSplit and then scales outer damage. The independent transferred damage uses a skipped reception path; this is not evidence that every damage transfer should re-enter ordinary reception.",
      "template": "skadi2_s_1[protect]",
      "basis": "current native method and existing case 03"
    },
    {
      "id": "hp-commit-and-notifications",
      "claim": "DoApplyModifier reads current HP and records its own applied delta. SetHpInternal includes lethal prevention and HP-zero handling. Ordinary OnAppliedModifier notifies the target container before source OnAfterOutputDamage. Death-related intervention cannot all be postponed until after success notifications.",
      "anchors": [
        "0x1806f1ce2",
        "0x1806f202f",
        "0x1806fd62c",
        "0x1806fd7cf",
        "0x1806f699b",
        "0x1806f6c38"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "PRTS 伤判效果 generalizes ignore-dodge as cancellation immunity, while 特殊机制 distinguishes ignoring dodge from inability to cancel by dodge. The ordinary native Evade path examined here rolls before cancellation permission is checked. Do not infer one universal RNG/charge behavior from these labels.",
    "Zero is rejected on the ordinary native input path; this is not a claim that zero HP loss means no HIT SP recovery.",
    "Full rebirth, negative-HP, kill attribution and object recycling are not exhaustively audited here.",
    "Current source/tests are project behavior, not client evidence. Historical case 03 contains superseded project architecture and inherited hook candidate policy; those sections do not override current independent-dispatch contracts."
  ],
